NAME
       chattr - change the special attributes of files on ext4 and xfs

SYNOPSIS
       chattr [-R] [-V] +ATTRS|-ATTRS|=ATTRS FILE...

DESCRIPTION
       Besides the normal permissions, files on Linux file systems can carry
       attributes that even root has to respect. chattr adds (+), removes (-)
       or sets exactly (=) them. lsattr shows them. Only root may set i and a.

       The two that matter most:

       i      immutable: the file cannot be changed, renamed, deleted or
              linked to, by anyone, until the attribute is removed.

       a      append only: data can be added to the end, nothing else.

OPTIONS
       -R     Work on directories and their contents.

       -V     Report what is done.

EXAMPLES
       Protect a file from changes, then allow them again:

           chattr +i /etc/resolv.conf
           lsattr /etc/resolv.conf
           chattr -i /etc/resolv.conf

SEE ALSO
       lsattr(1), chmod(1)
